/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Event Delegation in full technical detail, illustrating how to implement a high-performance delegated list handler.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Event Delegation is an architectural pattern that leverages Event Bubbling to manage events at) Tj
T*
(   a parent level rather than binding individual listeners to each child element:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Problem:) Tj
T*
(   In a dynamic application with a table or list of 5,000 items, binding an event listener to) Tj
T*
(   every single row consumes megabytes of heap memory and slows page initialization. Furthermore,) Tj
T*
(   new rows added dynamically via AJAX require manual event rebinding.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Delegated Solution:) Tj
T*
(   Attach a SINGLE listener to the static parent container \(`<ul>`\). When any child item is) Tj
T*
(   clicked, the event bubbles up to the parent, which inspects `event.target`:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   const todoList = document.getElementById\('todoList'\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   todoList.addEventListener\('click', function\(e\) {) Tj
T*
(   // Find closest button or delete action) Tj
T*
(   const deleteBtn = e.target.closest\('.delete-btn'\);) Tj
T*
(   if \(deleteBtn && todoList.contains\(deleteBtn\)\) {) Tj
T*
ET

