(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the IntersectionObserver API, detailing its configuration options and demonstrating an image lazy-loading script.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Historically, detecting when an element scrolled into view required listening to window) Tj
T*
(   'scroll' events and repeatedly calling `getBoundingClientRect\(\)`, causing severe main-thread) Tj
T*
(   layout thrashing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   IntersectionObserver Solution:) Tj
T*
(   Asynchronously monitors the intersection of a target element with an ancestor viewport) Tj
T*
(   container:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   const imgObserver = new IntersectionObserver\(\(entries, observer\) => {) Tj
T*
(   entries.forEach\(entry => {) Tj
T*
(   if \(entry.isIntersecting\) {) Tj
T*
(   const img = entry.target;) Tj
T*
(   img.src = img.dataset.src; // Swap placeholder with real image) Tj
T*
(   img.classList.remove\('lazy'\);) Tj
T*
(   observer.unobserve\(img\); // Stop observing loaded image) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }\);) Tj
T*
(   }, {) Tj
T*
(   root: null, // Viewport) Tj
T*
(   rootMargin: '0px 0px 200px 0px', // Pre-load 200px before scrolling into view) Tj
T*
(   threshold: 0.1 // 10% visible) Tj
T*
(   }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   document.querySelectorAll\('img.lazy'\).forEach\(img => imgObserver.observe\(img\)\);) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
