(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the ResizeObserver API, compare it with window.onresize, and demonstrate responsive component card resizing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The `ResizeObserver` API monitors changes to the content or border box dimensions of individual) Tj
T*
(   DOM elements independently of the browser window:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Why Window.onresize is Insufficient:) Tj
T*
(   `window.onresize` fires only when the global browser window is resized. It does not fire when a) Tj
T*
(   container's width changes due to sidebar toggling, CSS grid shifts, or font loads.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ResizeObserver Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   ```javascript) Tj
T*
(   const cardObserver = new ResizeObserver\(entries => {) Tj
T*
(   for \(const entry of entries\) {) Tj
T*
(   const width = entry.contentRect.width;) Tj
T*
(   const card = entry.target;) Tj
T*
(   if \(width < 350\) {) Tj
T*
(   card.classList.add\('card-compact'\);) Tj
T*
(   card.classList.remove\('card-expanded'\);) Tj
T*
(   } else {) Tj
T*
(   card.classList.add\('card-expanded'\);) Tj
T*
(   card.classList.remove\('card-compact'\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
(   }\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   document.querySelectorAll\('.dashboard-widget'\).forEach\(el => cardObserver.observe\(el\)\);) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
