(   [Problem Statement]: Explain JavaScript Event Bubbling traps when working with nested elements and how to handle event.target vs event.currentTarget.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   A common bug in DOM programming arises from misunderstanding `event.target` vs) Tj
T*
(   `event.currentTarget`:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Distinction:) Tj
T*
(   - `event.target`: The exact innermost element clicked by the user \(which could be an `<i>` icon) Tj
T*
(   or `<span>` inside a button\).) Tj
T*
(   - `event.currentTarget`: The element to which the event listener was actually attached.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Bug:) Tj
T*
(   If you bind a click listener to `<button class="btn"><i class="icon"></i> Submit</button>` and) Tj
T*
(   read `e.target.dataset.id`, clicking the icon returns `undefined` because `e.target` is the) Tj
T*
(   `<i>` element.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   The Robust Fix:) Tj
T*
(   Use `event.currentTarget` \(guaranteed to be the button\) OR `event.target.closest\('button'\)`:) Tj
T*
ET

